| 900 | under walk, writing a rope (a string past 32 characters made by `\|\|`) to a `FileWriteStream` stops the run: "Unification error: Closure/Constructor for writeOn param 1 (stream:WriteStream) got arg <Write handle to …> of type FileWriteStream", at `Library/File.fss:79` | NEGATIVE-VERIFIED | library bug (library) | silent | none | review io-objects-carrier-2026-11-06 | siblings: 901. `FileWriteStream` extends only `FileStream` (`Library/File.fsi:102`, `Library/File.fss:66`, at c141e7f6a), not `WriteStream`, so `write(x:String)`'s `x.writeOn(self)` (`Library/File.fss:79`) finds no `writeOn` that takes it. A flat string writes. `bin/fortress` on `o.write("a rope: abc…xyz" \|\| "ABC…XYZ\n")`: the error quoted, rc=1. Fix: extend `WriteStream`, a step that option (b) of `explorations/reviews/io-objects-carrier-2026-11-06.md` (point 16) allows and its rung may leave out; `WriteStream` declares `abstract flush()` (`Library/Stream.fsi:64`), which the object lacks (row 901). |
| 901 | the one library's `FileWriteStream` has no `flush()`, though `Library/File.fsi:131` declares it: under walk `o.flush()` stops the run, "Cannot find definition for method flush given receiver <Write handle to …>" | NEGATIVE-VERIFIED | library bug (library) | silent | none | review io-objects-carrier-2026-11-06 | siblings: 841, 900. `object FileWriteStream` in `Library/File.fss:66` declares no `flush`, at c141e7f6a; walk does not check a component against its api (row 841). Extending `WriteStream` (row 900) asks for it too: `abstract flush()`, `Library/Stream.fsi:64`. `bin/fortress` on `o = FileWriteStream("out"); o.write("x\n"); o.flush()`: the error quoted, rc=1. |
| 747 | the compiled checker types `fail`'s result-only `T` at its bound `Any` in the `else` of an `if` with a generator clause inside a reduction's body, 'ZZ32->ZZ32 is not applicable to an argument of type Any' | NEGATIVE-BOUNDED | implementation gap (checker) | silent | `explorations/perf-probes/integer-power/REPORT.md` | integer-power probe | siblings: 560, 642, 438. Its site, `strToInt`'s `SUM[\ZZ32\]`, now writes `fail[\ZZ32\]` (`Library/FortressLibrary.fss:4597`, at c124c6b65), so no stage shows it; its body was `if d <- digit(s[i], radix) then d radix^(n-i) else fail("…") end` (`fail[\T\]`, `Library/FortressLibrary.fsi:37`). The measure: the count stage on a copy with `fail(` there, in a seeded worktree; not run since `0856f3e6a`. Which context drops the expected type is not traced. Workaround: `fail[\T\]`. No compiled reproducer: `if d <- e` is refused first, 'Variable __cond is not defined' (`ProjectFortress/compiler_tests/XXXIfGeneratorClause.test`); program: `rung-integer-power/REPORT.md` §8. full text: history, row 747 |
| 49 | an array literal with no declared type is not built into an array under walk: an untyped binding fails with `Can't infer element type for array construction`, and a literal in argument position is passed on as a paste, an `IUOTuple` never built into an array | NEGATIVE-VERIFIED | implementation gap (walk) | `Specification/basic/expressions/aggregate.tex`, "Array Expressions" | `ProjectFortress/tests/XXXArrayLiteralArgRungC.fss` | ours, run-c3, climb batch 3 rung C | siblings: 104, 142. `LHSEvaluator.forLValue` builds the array only from a declared type; with none it reports the error, the join of the element types left as a comment (`LHSEvaluator.java:140-145`, at c124c6b65). `Evaluator.forArrayElements` returns the paste, an `IUOTuple` (`Evaluator.java:854-861`), so `3 - [1 2]` fails dispatch with `(1,2): (Int,Int)`. `RR64` elements fail as a user type's do. The specification types the literal `Arrayk[\T, 0, n0, …, 0, nk-1\]` (`Array1` to `Array3` in the library), `T` the union of the element types. Workaround: a literal-sized type, `x: ZZ32[2] = [1 2]` or `sc: Vector[\RR64,3\] = [1.0 2.0 3.0]`. full text: history, row 49 |
| 106 | a paste whose block grid has a single row **or** a single column of matrix elements always fails the extent check: `[ A B ]`, `[ A ; B ]`, `[ h1 h2 h3 h4 ]`, square blocks included | NEGATIVE-VERIFIED | implementation gap (walk) | `Specification/basic/expressions/aggregate.tex`, "Array Expressions" | none | run-b, run-b2, run-c3 | siblings: 107. `Element at [0] has extent 2 along axis 1 but an earlier element has length 0`. `IUOTuple.finish` fills `extents` with `-1` for no constraint (`IUOTuple.java:116-122`, at c124c6b65) but leaves `extentSums` at zero (`:113`); an axis outside `extents.length` takes the `extentSums` branch (`:199-205`), whose `current < 0` guard never fires. `[a b c]` of three matrices fails alike, untyped or `Array[\Any,ZZ32\]`. Workaround: `tabulate` over an index map; for matrices, `array[\Any\](n)` with puts or varargs (row 130). Probes `explorations/run-b2/probes/g1d_paste1.fss` and `explorations/run-b2/probes/g1d_hcat.fss`, in the parent of `22ea0cd90`. full text: history, row 106 |
| 142 | a typed array literal as a **top-level** declaration is bound as a tuple: `shp: Vector[\ZZ32,9\] = [27 16 27 …]` fails with `Type mismatch binding (27,16,…)`, while the same declaration inside a function body works | NEGATIVE-VERIFIED | implementation gap (walk) | `Specification/basic/expressions/aggregate.tex`, "Array Expressions"; `Specification/basic/variables.tex`, "Top-Level Variable Declarations" | none | run-c | siblings: 49, 104. At top level the literal is never built into an array: `BuildEnvironments.forVarDecl4` checks the evaluated paste against the declared type (`BuildEnvironments.java:780-794`, at c124c6b65); only `LHSEvaluator.forLValue`, in a body, builds it. `p08a` gives `Type mismatch binding (27,16,…): (Int,Int,…) (type (Int,Int,…)) to shp (type Vector[\ZZ32,9\])`, `p08b` the same with `RR64[9]`, `p08c` (commas) `Operator [_] is not defined.`; `p08d`, in a function body, prints the array. Workaround: `array[\ZZ32\](9).tabulate(fn …)`, or the literal in a function. Probes `explorations/run-c/probes/p08a_literal.fss` to `p08d`, in the parent of `4ebf80aec`. full text: history, row 142 |
